    "field": "climate change",
    "problem": "Existing climate models and CO2 emission scenarios focus on the final target concentration of greenhouse gases, largely ignoring how the *rate* of CO2 increase critically affects the stability of the thermohaline circulation and its potential for collapse.",
    "method": "This paper uses a simple coupled atmosphere-ocean climate model to investigate how the stability of the thermohaline circulation is influenced by the rate of atmospheric CO2 increase, in addition to the final concentration attained.",
    "task": "The task is to use a climate model to investigate how the rate of atmospheric CO\u2082 increase, not just the final concentration, influences the stability of the Atlantic thermohaline circulation and its potential for collapse.",
